swin3d_b geometry (vision15/models/video/swin_transformer.py): patch_size=('2', '4', '4'), window_size=('8', '7', '7')

INPUT CLIP                                            STAGE-1 TOKENS
----------------------------------------------------------------------
E3AD stage 2, as wired (ImageQueue 4x3x736x1280)             117,760
standard Swin3D-B Kinetics clip (16x3x224x224)                25,088
the commented-out 224 centre-crop, 4 frames                    6,272

As-wired / standard-Kinetics token ratio :   4.69x
As-wired / commented-out-crop  ratio    :  18.78x

Swin window attention is ~linear in token count, so the per-sample cost of the
cognition branch is roughly the ratio above times a full Swin3D-B forward pass,
added to every nuScenes sample at both train and test time.
Paper Tab. 1 reports the E3AD(VAD-Base) FPS cost as 3.8 -> 3.7 (2.6%).
